  "worked_solution": "We can parameterize $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t \\\\ 5\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi )\n$$\n\nTo calculate the outward-pointing normal vector of a closed, positively oriented curve, we follow three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: We compute the tangent vector ${r}^{\u2032}(t).$\n\nDifferentiating the expression for $r(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{\u2032}(t) \\\\ {y}^{\u2032}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Since $C$ is oriented counterclockwise, we rotate ${r}^{\u2032}(t)$ by ${90}^{\u2218}$ *clockwise* to obtain an outward-pointing normal vector.\n\nThe rotation matrix that corresponds to a ${90}^{\u2218}$ clockwise rotation is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRotating the vector ${r}^{\u2032}(t)$ by ${90}^{\u2218}$ clockwise, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t \\\\ 5\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Finally, we normalize the vector found in step 2.\n\nNote that the magnitude of the vector found in step 2 equals the magnitude of ${r}^{\u2032}(t)$ (since they differ only by a rotation).\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n||{r}^{\u2032}(t)||=\\sqrt{(-5\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t)^{2}+(5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t)^{2}}=5,\n$$\n\nand since for our curve $x(t)=5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t$ and $y(t)=5\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t,$ it follows that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{1}{||{r}^{\u2032}(t)||}[\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t \\\\ 5\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t \\\\ 5\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
